1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,248
This deep-dive explains how Docentric Copilot turns a brief into a checked Word document, what changed in version zero thirteen, and where the honest boundaries are.

2
00:00:10,248 --> 00:00:12,694
The pipeline is deliberately boring.

3
00:00:12,694 --> 00:00:27,096
The parser normalizes the schema, the reference inspector builds evidence, the planner emits a typed Template IR, the validator checks structure, semantics and logic, and only then does the compiler produce DOCX.

4
00:00:27,096 --> 00:00:29,741
The schema layer is not a prompt dump.

5
00:00:29,741 --> 00:00:34,682
The parser records controls, types, collection scope and sample values.

6
00:00:34,682 --> 00:00:44,496
The planner receives bounded candidates with evidence, so a field can be recommended, but only the validator decides whether a path is legal.

7
00:00:44,496 --> 00:00:51,115
The planner emits a typed Template IR or a compact transport representation that expands into it.

8
00:00:51,115 --> 00:01:00,600
Compact mode is not a second document model; it is schema-validated, expanded deterministically, and repaired only within a bounded budget.

9
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:02,182
Validation is layered.

10
00:01:02,182 --> 00:01:15,700
Structural rules catch malformed blocks, schema rules reject unknown paths, semantic rules check the brief, and logic rules enforce condition scope, collection nesting and image placement.

11
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:19,008
A report is evidence, not an optimistic score.

12
00:01:19,008 --> 00:01:20,954
The compiler owns OOXML.

13
00:01:20,954 --> 00:01:29,551
It writes sections, headers, footers, tables, relationships and media, then packages a deterministic DOCX.

14
00:01:29,551 --> 00:01:37,824
The preview uses the same IR and inheritance rules, so preview and Word output do not drift by design.

15
00:01:37,824 --> 00:01:42,638
The deployed Streamlit demo was woken and exercised in Chromium.

16
00:01:42,638 --> 00:01:49,332
It reports version zero thirteen, commit one c b e zero seven three and IR one point two.

17
00:01:49,332 --> 00:01:57,456
Quotation, invoice and purchase order all download DOCX, and the hashes match the local deterministic build.

18
00:01:57,456 --> 00:02:01,970
Template IR is the contract between AI and deterministic code.

19
00:02:01,970 --> 00:02:09,687
Version one point two adds the first-page header, image source and fallback policy, and table footer rows.

20
00:02:09,687 --> 00:02:14,856
Older payloads migrate deterministically; unknown versions are refused.

21
00:02:14,856 --> 00:02:19,355
Images can come from schema data or from reviewed compile assets.

22
00:02:19,355 --> 00:02:22,816
Missing images follow an explicit fallback policy.

23
00:02:22,816 --> 00:02:33,336
The validator rejects wrong types and images outside the active collection scope, and the compiler preserves aspect ratio unless stretching is explicit.

24
00:02:33,336 --> 00:02:38,943
Table inference reads bounded DOCX geometry and joins it to schema evidence.

25
00:02:38,943 --> 00:02:47,943
It handles static headers, repeated rows, optional conditional cells, footer rows and a nested repeat under the outer row.

26
00:02:47,943 --> 00:02:53,328
Merged, ragged or ambiguous tables are blocking diagnostics, not guesses.

27
00:02:53,328 --> 00:02:57,941
The first-page header is a real Word header part selected by titlePg.

28
00:02:57,941 --> 00:03:08,304
Each IR section becomes a Word section; a null header inherits the previous section, an empty list clears it, and the preview follows the same inheritance.

29
00:03:08,304 --> 00:03:13,140
The reference evaluation is separate from the gold semantic benchmark.

30
00:03:13,140 --> 00:03:18,460
Seventeen official documents parse, sixteen reach import and fifteen compile.

31
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:26,544
The two remaining pipeline failures are classified: an unenclosed nested collection and an unsupported-only document.

32
00:03:26,544 --> 00:03:31,792
The final benchmark uses thirty-two cases, three providers and three repeats.

33
00:03:31,792 --> 00:03:42,016
Two hundred seventy-eight runs completed, ten Gemini structured-output failures remain technical, and two hundred seventy-four runs pass semantically.

34
00:03:42,016 --> 00:03:47,400
Precision is zero point nine five one and total spend is four dollars eighteen.

35
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:58,404
Every change passes lint, typing, unit tests with an eighty-five percent coverage gate, browser E2E, a real LibreOffice visual diff and security analysis.

36
00:03:58,404 --> 00:04:03,120
The release workflow builds and verifies the wheel and the images.

37
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:08,120
The demo runs on a deterministic mock provider and never needs a model key.

38
00:04:08,120 --> 00:04:15,520
Artifact uploads are bounded and signature-checked, provider errors are sanitized, and logs redact credentials.

39
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:21,120
The benchmark records spend and technical failures separately from semantic quality.

40
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:27,943
The release is backed by a wheel, source archive, CI, visual diffs and a published evidence page.

41
00:04:27,943 --> 00:04:34,977
The deployed demo is verified, but Word for the web and the final videos remain external open tasks.

42
00:04:34,977 --> 00:04:39,408
Those gaps stay visible instead of being converted into a pass.

43
00:04:39,408 --> 00:04:41,504
Read the benchmark carefully.

44
00:04:41,504 --> 00:04:46,779
Technical failures are excluded from semantic scoring but still reported.

45
00:04:46,779 --> 00:04:54,150
An accepted table means the inference layer produced IR, not that Microsoft Word renders it perfectly.

46
00:04:54,150 --> 00:04:58,920
A semantic pass is not a Docentric AX runtime compatibility proof.

47
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:14,745
The remaining gaps are external or explicit: Word for the web needs a human with Microsoft 365, videos need review and publishing, AT-07 remains partial, and Docentric AX runtime compatibility remains not tested.

48
00:05:14,745 --> 00:05:18,552
No semantic score is a runtime compatibility proof.
